  "worked_solution": "First, we write the images of vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1})=-2{c}_{1}+4{c}_{2}-2{c}_{3} & \\,\u27f9\\,[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2})=3{c}_{2}-7{c}_{3}+{c}_{1} & \\,\u27f9\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and  $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
